# check: fail a task is not handed x[i]: the element is copied here, and the copy would not last until the join
# E31b/P2: a call on a handle element runs on a copy of the handle held in the spawner's block - which closes, or is
# made again by the next turn of a loop, before the join; a function taking the collection does "x[i].Push(v)" itself
fn main() ? {
    users := List<List<I64>>()
    for i in range 4 { users.Push(List<I64>()) }
    join {
        for i in range 4 { spawn users[i].Push(i) }
    }
}
